                                                            <a href="~/WSP/Wsp_form">
                                                                <span> <img src="~/Content/WspImages/water balancing.jpg" id="img2Hover" /></span>
                                                                <label>Water Budgeting </label>
                                                            </a>
                                                        </li>
                                                        <li class="col-md-8">
                                                            <p class="sometext">
                                                                Water budgeting helps to quantify the hydrologic cycle. A water
                                                                budget is an accounting of the rates of water movement and the change in water
                                                                storage in all or parts of the atmosphere, land surface, and sub-surface. It gives an
                                                                account of all the water that flows into and out of an area. The main function of water
                                                                budgeting tool is to estimate the amount of water a landscape will have, based on its
                                                                recharge and draft capacity. Water budget takes into account reference rainfall data,
                                                                irrigated landscape area, water sources data and, the purpose and functionality of
                                                                the landscape. It can be calculated for daily, monthly and annual irrigation event.
                                                            </p>

                                                        </li>
                                                    </ul>
                                                </div>
